{"title":"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems\">2009 AMC 10B #23</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems\">2009 AMC 12B #18</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#MANIM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">MANIM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Video_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Video solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Interval_Intersection)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Interval Intersection)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rachel and Robert run on a circular track.  Rachel runs counterclockwise and completes a lap every 90 seconds, and Robert runs clockwise and completes a lap every 80 seconds.  Both start from the same line at the same time.  At some random time between 10 minutes and 11 minutes after they begin to run, a photographer standing inside the track takes a picture that shows one-fourth of the track, centered on the starting line.  What is the probability that both Rachel and Robert are in the picture?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c50102db0750173a6242ce3b2db3d4eb7f9ee28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\frac {1}{16}\\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\frac 18\\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\frac {3}{16}\\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\frac 14\\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\frac {5}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"360\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce3b33448115127f15871da09d1ab63a1cddd435.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> seconds<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/f/b8ff48facb2d169243b88fba455ef6c48e0b0504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"18\" /> Rachel will have completed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> laps and be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds from completing her seventh lap. Because Rachel runs one-fourth of a lap in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d413c0964b8ba3371f882fd21fa87baeb74e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22.5$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> seconds, she will be in the picture between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6af17885838cfff31a3105dbea2d198fd16788df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> seconds and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42ca2a2ba7ab76e1101c3f3aeb5775c4035e1df9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> seconds of the tenth minute.  After 10 minutes, Robert will have completed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> laps and be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds from completing his eighth lap.  Because Robert runs one-fourth of a lap in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds, he will be in the picture between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds of the tenth minute.  Hence both Rachel and Robert will be in the picture if it is taken between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42ca2a2ba7ab76e1101c3f3aeb5775c4035e1df9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> seconds of the tenth minute.  So the probability that both runners are in the picture is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/d/6ed529199646ae67b9a04dd4b29b4387bf770b70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {41.25 - 30} {60} = \\boxed{\\frac {3}{16}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"144\" height=\"48\" />.  The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/2484f88154fadcf9c781bba19becdae88696b77f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/syoyurIkDnI\">https://youtu.be/syoyurIkDnI</a>\n~MathInMotionPy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"MANIM\">MANIM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: MANIM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Edm18JTXvdg\">https://youtu.be/Edm18JTXvdg</a>\n~MathInMotionPy\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Video_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Video_solution)\">Solution 2 (Video solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Video solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Video: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/eZjJ5MQV47o\">https://youtu.be/eZjJ5MQV47o</a>\n~DaBobWhoLikeMath\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Interval_Intersection.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Interval_Intersection)\">Solution 3 (Interval Intersection)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Interval Intersection)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Convert the problem's time frames into absolute time in seconds, where the photographer's window spans from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/d/27d52375448f3a963779d87060451b686834937d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\text{ minutes} = 600 \\text{ seconds}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"194\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3e1f95808ca0625fdd0458c6543cfe1494e540b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\text{ minutes} = 660 \\text{ seconds}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"194\" height=\"14\" />. This gives a total sample space of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/5/af5c3f83a4a50c83aa8749104f6eac5f084afa4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$660 - 600 = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" /> seconds.\n</p><p>The photograph covers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the track centered directly on the starting line. A runner appears in the frame if they are within <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of a lap before or after the starting line. We can find the specific time windows where each runner is captured during this minute:\n<br />\n</p>\n<ul><li>Rachel's Frame Window: Rachel completes a full lap every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds. Within the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab29bad55543e42835d17bcc5c3dec44e4347ab3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600\\text{--}660$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> second interval, she crosses the starting line exactly at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3af53c7ab46ab18094c6076d42afcdb4d3cd08a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 630$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> seconds (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/4177d3d7d5593762c2b9f1af5d69e8711ec6d7a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\times 90 = 630$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />). Since she takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b38fea6ee6180ba222e821f92b4e76c9ceb73a3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8} \\times 90 = 11.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"121\" height=\"38\" /> seconds to cover <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of a lap, she is visible in the frame from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c67dcc2fabdc566526c4dd855472299181f9af06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> seconds before crossing to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c67dcc2fabdc566526c4dd855472299181f9af06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> seconds after:</li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/4565c03c73e59198aed4df2e3263f34fe0158fc2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[630 - 11.25, 630 + 11.25] = [618.75, 641.25]\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"18\" />\n<br />\n</p>\n<ul><li>Robert's Frame Window: Robert completes a full lap every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds. Within the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab29bad55543e42835d17bcc5c3dec44e4347ab3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600\\text{--}660$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> second interval, he crosses the starting line exactly at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af374fc53cbd32e66d4a1ff951ffd33057d0e3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 640$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> seconds (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb838e7507507351dc53b58dbf8b8a3cd69fc93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\times 80 = 640$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />). Since he takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b31473a8ed190b6925d320916261db8bc47807bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8} \\times 80 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" /> seconds to cover <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of a lap, he is visible in the frame from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds before crossing to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds after:</li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/16495e2453bb7d709362ac11c886a753c80386fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[640 - 10, 640 + 10] = [630, 650]\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"18\" />\n<br />\nTo find the time where both runners are simultaneously in the picture, we take the intersection of their individual intervals by selecting the most restrictive bounds:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42b2c5a288b6da556790733624c20e09d8f65a54.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Intersection} = [618.75, 641.25] \\cap [630, 650] = [630, 641.25]\\]\" width=\"439\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The total duration of this overlapping success window is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/9/76963c8172a14418dc14137ec462f2181e2f588a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$641.25 - 630 = 11.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"15\" /> seconds. \n</p><p>Dividing this successful interval by the total <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-second photo span yields the target probability:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/8/3e8092797415c3f2a05fa41e736f2394ca1c250f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P = \\frac{11.25}{60} = \\frac{1125}{6000} = \\frac{45}{240} = \\boxed{\\text{(C) } \\frac{3}{16}}\\]\" width=\"292\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~Sunsine\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B\">2009 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" t